Prototype getenv and getopt so make builds with GCC 15 against musl.

make 4.4.1 still carries three K&R declarations that GCC 15 rejects.
GCC 15 compiles C as gnu23 unless told otherwise (gcc/c-family/c-opts.cc:
"The default for C is gnu23"), and in C23 an empty parameter list is a
prototype that takes no arguments. GCC's own manual says so under
-Wdeprecated-non-prototype: calling a function declared with an empty
parameter list, or defining it with parameters afterwards, are "both cases
errors in C23 and later dialects of C".

lib/fnmatch.c and src/getopt.c declare

    extern char *getenv ();

and then call getenv with one argument, which is the first of those two
errors. Prototyping the declaration to match stdlib.h is enough.

src/getopt.h is the half that is specific to this target. The prototyped
getopt declaration there sits behind #ifdef __GNU_LIBRARY__, with an
unprototyped

    extern int getopt ();

in the #else arm, because the comment above it only wants a prototype for
the GNU C library. glibc defines __GNU_LIBRARY__ unconditionally in
features.h; musl does not define it at all. So a glibc build takes the
prototyped arm and compiles, and a musl build takes the unprototyped one
and then hits src/getopt.c defining getopt with three parameters, which is
the second of the two C23 errors. Hadron builds everything against musl, so
Hadron is where it fails. Deleting the conditional leaves the prototype the
comment says the GNU C library wants, which is also the only declaration
that matches the definition in this tarball.

Not reported upstream from here. GNU make's tree still carries all three
declarations, so the fix is wanted there and nobody has sent it; whoever
picks this up should report it to bug-make@gnu.org. Drop this patch once a
make release prototypes them, which is visible as the hunks below failing to
apply.

--- a/lib/fnmatch.c
+++ b/lib/fnmatch.c
@@ -121,7 +121,7 @@
    whose names are inconsistent.  */
 
 # if !defined _LIBC && !defined getenv
-extern char *getenv ();
+extern char *getenv (const char *);
 # endif
 
 # ifndef errno
--- a/src/getopt.c
+++ b/src/getopt.c
@@ -202,7 +202,7 @@
    whose names are inconsistent.  */
 
 #ifndef getenv
-extern char *getenv ();
+extern char *getenv (const char *);
 #endif
 
 static char *
--- a/src/getopt.h
+++ b/src/getopt.h
@@ -96,14 +96,10 @@
 #define optional_argument	2
 
 #if defined (__STDC__) && __STDC__
-#ifdef __GNU_LIBRARY__
 /* Many other libraries have conflicting prototypes for getopt, with
    differences in the consts, in stdlib.h.  To avoid compilation
    errors, only prototype getopt for the GNU C library.  */
 extern int getopt (int argc, char *const *argv, const char *shortopts);
-#else /* not __GNU_LIBRARY__ */
-extern int getopt ();
-#endif /* __GNU_LIBRARY__ */
 extern int getopt_long (int argc, char *const *argv, const char *shortopts,
 		        const struct option *longopts, int *longind);
 extern int getopt_long_only (int argc, char *const *argv,
